<title>Equilibria in discrete dynamical systems</title>

<p><ref>Video 1</ref> | <ref>Video 2</ref> | <ref>Video 3</ref> | <ref>Transcripts</ref> </p>


<p>Finding equilibria when the dynamical system has unspecified parameters can lead to new subtleties.  As shown in this video, the number of equilibria could depend on the value of the parameters.</p>

<section><title>Video 3</title>


<figure suppressFigureNameInCaption="true">
<video youtube="QvXyeHCHt5w" size="large" aspectRatio="16/9" name="v1" />
<caption>Equilibria of discrete dynamical systems with parameters. </caption>
</figure>

 
<number name="v1RoundUp" hide="true">
  <conditionalContent>
    <case condition="$v1.fractionWatched > 0.9">1</case>
    <else>$v1.fractionWatched</else>
  </conditionalContent>
</number>
  
  <p>Video credit achieved: <number displayDecimals="1">$v1RoundUp*100</number>%</p>

<answer hide="true" name="v1Credit">
  <award credit="$v1RoundUp"><when>true</when></award>
</answer>

<callAction triggerWith="$v1" target="$v1Credit" actionName="submitAnswer" />


  <problem><title>Video review question</title>

  <p>Find the equilibria of the dynamical system <m>x_{t+1} - x_{t} = a x_t - 1</m>, where <m>a</m> is a non-zero constant parameter.</p>

  <p>How many equilibria are there? <answer name="n">1</answer></p>

  <hint hide="$n.creditAchieved = 1 or $n.numSubmissions &lt; 2">
    <p>There is 1 one equilibrium.</p>
  </hint>

  <p>The equilibria are:
    <repeatForSequence length="min(5,$n)" name="Es">
        <p>
          <m>x_t = </m> <mathInput />
        </p>
      </repeatForSequence>
  </p>
  <answer name="ansEs" matchPartial="true">
    <award>
      <when><mathList>
        <setup><collect componentType="mathInput" from="$Es" name="collect_list" /></setup><mathList name="list" extend="$collect_list.value" />
      </mathList> = <math>1/a</math></when>
    </award>
  </answer>

  <hint hide="$ansEs.creditAchieved = 1 or $ansEs.numSubmissions &lt; 2 or $ansEs.numSubmissions >= 5">
    <p>Plug in <m>x_{t+1} = E</m> and <m>x_t = E</m> into the dynamical system, obtaining the equation <m>E - E = aE -1</m>.</p>
    <p>To determine the equilibria, solve for <m>E</m>.</p>
  </hint>


  <hint hide="$ansEs.creditAchieved = 1 or $ansEs.numSubmissions &lt; 5">
    <p>Plug in <m>x_{t+1} = E</m> and <m>x_t = E</m> into the dynamical system, obtaining the equation <m>E - E = aE -1</m>.</p>
    <p>To determine the equilibria, solve for <m>E</m>.  Simplify the equation to <m>0=aE-1</m> and add 1 to both sides, yielding <m>1=aE</m>.  Divide both sides by <m>a</m> (which is OK since we were given that <m>a \ne 0</m>) to determine that <m>E = \frac{1}{a}</m>The one equilibrium is <m>x_t = \frac{1}{a}</m>.</p>
  </hint>


  <solution>
    <p>Plug in <m>x_{t+1} = E</m> and <m>x_t = E</m> into the dynamical system, obtaining the equation <m>E - E = aE -1</m>.</p>
    <p>To determine the equilibria, solve for <m>E</m>.  Simplify the equation to <m>0=aE-1</m> and add 1 to both sides, yielding <m>1=aE</m>.  Divide both sides by <m>a</m> (which is OK since we were given that <m>a \ne 0</m>) to determine that <m>E = \frac{1}{a}</m>The one equilibrium is <m>x_t = \frac{1}{a}</m>.</p>
  </solution>
    
  </problem>   

  
<p>For a graphical approach to finding the equilibria see 
<ref to="doenet:7FRM6VWrzPKk1bwC2SKx72">a graphical approach to finding equilibria of discrete dynamical systems</ref>.</p>

  
</section>